  "body": {
    "id": "prop:positive-band-high-s-minimax",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Let \\(s=(\\alpha+\\beta)/2\\) and \\(s_0=d\\gamma/\\{2(2\\gamma+d)\\}\\).  For every compact\n\\[\n K\\subset\\mathcal R_{\\mathrm{pair}}\\cap\\{(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma):s\\geq s_0\\},\n\\]\nthere are \\(0<c_K\\leq C_K<\\infty\\) and \\(n_K\\) such that, uniformly over \\((\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma)\\in K\\) and \\(n\\geq n_K\\),\n\\[\n c_Kn^{-\\gamma/(2\\gamma+d)}\n \\leq\n \\inf_{\\widetilde\\tau_n}\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{band}}}\n \\mathbb E_P|\\widetilde\\tau_n(O_{1:n})-\\tau_P(x_0)|\n \\leq C_Kn^{-\\gamma/(2\\gamma+d)}.\n\\]\nThus, and only in this above-elbow regime, the displayed order is the proved positive-band minimax mean-absolute-risk rate.  If instead \\(K\\) is a compact subset of \\(\\mathcal R_{\\mathrm{pair}}\\cap\\{s<s_0\\}\\), the proved conclusions are only the honest bracket\n\\[\n c_Kn^{-\\gamma/(2\\gamma+d)}\n \\leq\n \\inf_{\\widetilde\\tau_n}\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal P_{\\mathrm{band}}}\n \\mathbb E_P|\\widetilde\\tau_n(O_{1:n})-\\tau_P(x_0)|\n \\leq C_Kn^{-1/\\{1+d/(2\\gamma)+d/(4s)\\}}.\n\\]\nThe matching positive-band low-smoothness converse remains unresolved.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "s",
      "\\alpha",
      "\\beta",
      "\\gamma",
      "d",
      "n",
      "O_{1:n}",
      "x_0",
      "P",
      "\\mathcal{P}_{\\mathrm{band}}",
      "\\mathcal{R}_{\\mathrm{pair}}",
      "\\tau_P"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
