      "thm:unified-benchmark-attainment"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "On a compact \\(K\\subset\\mathcal R_{\\mathrm{pair}}\\), \\(\\mathrm{thm:unified\\mbox{-}benchmark\\mbox{-}attainment}\\) supplies the explicit estimator \\(\\widehat\\tau_n^*(x_0)\\) and the upper bound \\(C_Kr_n^*\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{prop:optimizer\\mbox{-}elbow\\mbox{-}rate}\\), this is at most \\(C_Kn^{-\\gamma/(2\\gamma+d)}\\) when \\(s\\geq s_0\\), and at most \\(C_Kn^{-1/\\{1+d/(2\\gamma)+d/(4s)\\}}\\) when \\(s<s_0\\).  Since the infimum over all estimators is no larger than the risk of this particular total data-driven estimator, these are the two asserted upper bounds.  The lower bound in both regimes is \\(\\mathrm{thm:positive\\mbox{-}band\\mbox{-}oracle\\mbox{-}lower\\mbox{-}bound}\\).  The upper and lower powers coincide exactly when \\(s\\geq s_0\\).  Below the elbow they do not coincide; no larger-class support-hole lower bound is used to close that gap, because such a lower bound need not transfer to the positive-band subclass.",
